[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Stalwart has been installed as %%PREFIX%%/bin/stalwart.

1. Enable and start the service:

     sysrc stalwart_enable=YES
     service stalwart start

2. Without %%ETCDIR%%/config.json, Stalwart starts in bootstrap
   mode. It then only serves the setup WebUI at
   http://<hostname>:8080/admin on all addresses, and prints a
   temporary administrator password to /var/log/stalwart.log:

     grep -A8 'bootstrap mode' /var/log/stalwart.log

   To change this, add environment variables to stalwart_env before
   the first start, e.g.:

     sysrc stalwart_env+=STALWART_RECOVERY_ADMIN=admin:<password>
     sysrc stalwart_env+=STALWART_RECOVERY_MODE_BIND=127.0.0.1
     sysrc stalwart_env+=STALWART_RECOVERY_MODE_PORT=9090

   The WebUI itself is downloaded from GitHub at runtime.

3. Complete the setup in the WebUI. Stalwart writes its configuration
   to %%ETCDIR%%/config.json and its data to /var/db/stalwart.
   Then remove STALWART_RECOVERY_ADMIN from stalwart_env, if you set
   it, and restart the service:

     service stalwart restart

   Stalwart starts as root, binds its listeners and then runs as the
   user "%%USERS%%". Listeners on ports below 1024 that were added
   in the WebUI are only bound after a restart.

%%NO_ENTERPRISE%%This package was built without the ENTERPRISE option. Its data
%%NO_ENTERPRISE%%store cannot be opened by a build with the Enterprise features,
%%NO_ENTERPRISE%%such as upstream's binaries and container images, and vice versa.
%%ENTERPRISE%%This package was built with the ENTERPRISE option. The Enterprise
%%ENTERPRISE%%features are only enabled with a valid license key or API key,
%%ENTERPRISE%%set in the Enterprise settings of the WebUI. Without one,
%%ENTERPRISE%%Stalwart logs a warning for each affected setting and
%%ENTERPRISE%%- uses only the primary store of a SQL read replica setup,
%%ENTERPRISE%%- disables the metrics and tracing stores and LDAP failover,
%%ENTERPRISE%%- uses the default directory for all domains.
%%ENTERPRISE%%Sharded blob and in-memory stores stay in use.
%%ENTERPRISE%%
%%ENTERPRISE%%The data store cannot be opened by a build without the
%%ENTERPRISE%%ENTERPRISE option, and vice versa.

To migrate a Stalwart 0.16 installation (mail/stalwart016), use
%%NO_ENTERPRISE%%mail/stalwart-migrate.
%%ENTERPRISE%%mail/stalwart-migrate@enterprise.
EOM
}
{ type: upgrade
  maximum_version: "1.2.1"
  message: <<EOM
Stalwart 1.2.0 added new permissions that default roles created by an
earlier version do not include (mail rules, junk e-mail lists,
calendar settings and Exchange). If you upgraded from a version before
1.2.0 and have not added them yet, restart Stalwart once with:

  sysrc stalwart_env+=STALWART_UPDATE_ROLE_PERMISSIONS=true
  service stalwart restart
  sysrc stalwart_env-=STALWART_UPDATE_ROLE_PERMISSIONS=true

Also update the WebUI to version 2.1.1 or later.

See https://stalw.art/docs/auth/authorization/permissions#default-roles-on-upgraded-servers
EOM
}
]
